WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.000
What happens when you place bacon&nbsp;
and a photo of SCP-682 into SCP-914?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.240
Dr. Curtis decided to find out.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.800
One pound of fully cooked bacon and&nbsp;
a photograph of SCP-682 were placed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.600
into the Clockworks on the setting "Very Fine."

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.680
The output produced was a five-inch miniature&nbsp;
replica of SCP-682, made from bacon and photo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.800
paper. The object was able to move on its own&nbsp;
and displayed hostile behavior toward all life.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.440
Its small size prevented it from doing any damage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.440
but it did attempt to breach containment&nbsp;
and kill all staff in the vicinity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.400
When the creature moved, it produced a&nbsp;
sizzling sound like that of bacon in a hot pan.

